+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every registered tool declares a JSON Schema in `inputSchema` (`src/types/ai.ts`) that is sent to the active provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` (`src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts`) enforces that same schema before any tool executor runs. Validation happens once at the registry boundary so executors receive input that already satisfies their declared contract, while malformed model calls return structured rejection text inside the conversation loop rather than aborting the turn.
+
+## Validation boundary
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, enforcing `required`, declared property types, and `enum` without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, applying defaults, or coercing types; a rejected call returns a `ToolResponse` describing what failed without calling the executor, while valid input carrying unlisted extra properties passes through unchanged ([validated by: enforces required and enum schemas and passes unlisted keys through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+- Rejection `ToolResponse.result` strings and registry log lines name only the failing property paths and the constraint or expected type that failed, never any offending or identifying property value from `input` ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field without leaking input values in results or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` when no tool is registered under `name`; only a registered tool whose input fails schema validation returns a rejection `ToolResponse`.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled during `ToolRegistry.register`, throwing synchronously with an error message naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws naming the tool at registration time when a static schema is invalid](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L108)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration and reused across repeated `execute` calls rather than recompiled on each call.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved on each `execute` call and validated against the schema returned for that call rather than a stale schema from an earlier call ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool against the schema returned on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L127)).
+- A schema returned by a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is cached by resolved schema object reference so returning the same schema object across calls reuses its compiled validator.
+
+## Tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing out of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts`, the orchestrator forwards `result` to the provider as a `tool_result` block on the next round so the model can correct its call within the `maxToolRounds` bound and resolve `processMessage` ([validated by: returns a validation rejection to the provider so a retry resolves the turn](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L162)).
